     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is above the maximum and needs your confirmation first.\n\n**The problem:** Metformin 1700 mg three times a day adds up to **5100 mg/day**. The labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin is **2550 mg/day**, and for extended-release it's 2000 mg/day. This order is about twice the maximum. That raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI side effects, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**This may be a transcription error.** Two common orders that look similar:\n- **850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the IR maximum)\n- **1700 mg/day total**, given as 850 mg twice daily with meals\n\nCould you confirm which dose you meant? Also, is this immediate-release or extended-release? Once you reply, I'll enter the order right away."
